        <p class="profile-detail-region">City · South &amp; Southeast Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Lahore</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 982 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">No definitive record of its founding exists. Oral tradition says Lava, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a>, founded it; the first document to name the city is the Hudud al-'Alam of 982.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">In central-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ravi">Ravi</a> River, in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> close to the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Odi Shahi, Ghaznavid and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> capital; the Mughal capital under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>; the Lahore Fort, the Badshahi Mosque and the Shalimar Gardens; the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore-resolution">Lahore Resolution</a> of 1940; the riots of Partition in 1947</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Lahore is the capital of the Pakistani province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> and the second-largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, with a population of over 14 million.</span></div>
