    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Lahore rose to prominence in the late 10th century and served as a capital under the Odi Shahi dynasty, the Ghaznavids, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>.</li><li>Its Mughal monuments, among them the Lahore Fort, the Shalimar Gardens and the Badshahi Mosque, were built between the reigns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a>, and the city decayed in the 18th century under repeated Afghan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> contests.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> in 1849, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore-resolution">Lahore Resolution</a> of 1940 called for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, and the city suffered the worst riots of Partition in 1947 before becoming the capital of Pakistani Punjab.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Badshahi Mosque, raised in 1673 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a>, was the largest mosque in the world when it was built.</p></aside>
    </section>

